Pixelado layer on BananaDS (SuperDrastic bananads/), part 2 of 2.

- The Party's room survives DS Download Play: the emulator no longer stays stopped after
  the DS menu hands over to the downloaded game (stop_ is cleared before nds_->Start()).
- Rejoin after a network loss: a client that lost its host keeps that host's address and
  joins it again when it is heard (every 3 s, for up to 60 s).
- Real latency: a UDP echo on port 7065 (lanecho) measures each player's round trip;
  the Party shows the median of the last 5 replies. A client also reports its host's
  ping (LAN::GetHostPing, melonDS patch 0002).
- Menu choices last for the whole Party: the in-game menu's settings (FPS counter, 3D effects,
  shader, fast-forward speed) also reach the settings the running process already read, so the
  next game opened in the same process keeps them.

Applied with: patch -p1 -d <SuperDrastic tree>, after 0001.

